# Packages Architecture And Query Standards

- Keep process-layer data retrieval cohesive: prefer one optimized query per use case when practical.
- Do not introduce N+1 query patterns (for example, querying children inside a loop over parents).
- Prefer join-first retrieval with grouped aggregation for related entities when building list/detail responses.
- Select only required columns; avoid `select *` in package queries.
- Add a short rationale comment above complex multi-join or aggregate queries describing why this shape is used.
- Return stable structured objects from queries (for example, aggregated JSON fields for related entities) to reduce post-processing and extra round-trips.

## Good Pattern Example

Use the pattern in `packages/product/processes/product/paginated-products/paginated-products.process.ts`:
- joins product variants, category, and sales channels in one query
- aggregates related rows (`count`, `array_agg`, `jsonb_build_object`)
- groups once and returns consumer-ready fields
